# SPA fallback.
#
# /wiki is a real URL, so a reload or a pasted deep link asks the host for that
# path directly. A static host would 404 it without this; every unmatched path
# has to be served index.html and let the client router take over.
#
# The cost of getting this wrong is deferred and invisible: it works perfectly
# in the dev server, which already does this, and only breaks in production.
/*    /index.html   200
